p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"106406cc-f94b-48fd-83ba-5546ce317cdc","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":42,"LLM_1":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Where was the computer first invented?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The history of the computer is complex, as it wasn’t \"invented\" in a single moment by one person. Instead, it evolved through several stages. Depending on how you define a \"computer,\" here are the most important locations and creators:\n\n### 1. The Concept: England (1830s)\nThe theoretical foundation for the modern computer was laid in England by **Charles Babbage**. In the 1830s, he designed the **Analytical Engine**, which is considered the first design for a general-purpose electronic computer. While it was never built during his lifetime due to funding and mechanical limitations, its design included an Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU), control flow, and memory—the basic architecture of today's computers.\n\n### 2. The First Programmable Computer: Germany (1941)\nThe first functional, fully automatic, programmable computer, the **Z3**, was built by **Konrad Zuse** in **Berlin, Germany**. It was completed in 1941 and used binary floating-point numbers.\n\n### 3. The First Electronic Digital Computer: United States (1942–1945)\nIf you define a computer as an electronic, digital machine (the precursor to modern hardware), there are two primary claimants:\n\n*   **Atanasoff-Berry Computer (ABC):** Built between 1937 and 1942 at **Iowa State University** by John Vincent Atanasoff and Clifford Berry. It was the first to use electronic vacuum tubes and binary math, though it was not programmable.\n*   **ENIAC (Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer):** Built at the **University of Pennsylvania** in Philadelphia by J. Presper Eckert and John Mauchly. Completed in 1945, it was the first programmable, electronic, general-purpose digital computer that could solve a large class of numerical problems.\n\n### 4. The First Stored-Program Computer: England (1948)\nWhile the ENIAC was revolutionary, it had to be \"re-wired\" to change its tasks. The **Manchester Baby**, built at the **University of Manchester** in England, was the first computer to store its program in electronic memory (the \"stored-program\" architecture), which is how every computer works today.\n\n### Summary\n*   **The Idea:** England (Charles Babbage)\n*   **The First Programmable Machine:** Germany (Konrad Zuse)\n*   **The First Electronic Machine:** USA (Atanasoff-Berry Computer)\n*   **The First Modern-Architecture Machine:** England (Manchester Baby)\n\nIn short, the modern computer is the result of collaborative advancements made primarily across **England, Germany, and the United States** during the mid-20th century.","reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a18MyfYW780P7sGPYQfsKeMY/kH/PW6orLQkR+5ysksNDshBeZ451SIDwJJfne/TDej5Nn2kqIklHs4FTsq49lrUpBr1y2BPKFGp7TQ3FZk=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}}],"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a1+uFXOzu88T7fxV0L5e+vK41F+bRdoDSVT/UmcwEFFRbY8WyiEqDMsfSb4dKzb4iFdhSPJfmmzJ8ov8DqdSEMoq3M3YLpgEqzv1bXpTi+o=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},{"text":56,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":15},"llm":{"key":"02f487d0-004a-488c-b0e8-716165011454","name":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite","model":"google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"5dadc986-8ae6-4670-9e57-72e1ea7836e5","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":42,"LLM_1":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Is the Legend of Zelda a video game series?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes, **The Legend of Zelda** is a highly influential video game series created by Japanese game designers Shigeru Miyamoto and Takashi Tezuka. It is developed and published by Nintendo. \n\nFirst released in 1986, the series focuses on the adventures of a hero named Link, who typically must rescue Princess Zelda and save the kingdom of Hyrule from the antagonist, Ganon. It is well-known for mixing action, adventure, puzzle-solving, and exploration gameplay.","reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a1/OSYVLCWbHNvtbHVJkizVo2GqwRwufHYexyVQ7d4S6k8zbL6mYdkYrpgM817urhQ0pYv3UF3WK0Y4hsRe5z0NBnZ3BoMSlKl53rwSKMXk=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}}],"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a19FIeIoI9nzijWcZK8UoRfEDWNDG29elHILn7pMmENBeIIe+tN2Ew6I/UmAuh8ncYlHWbi5S6vQe7tw7jUtj1kYWgqMkEHvKksO/kCHWL4=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},{"text":65,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":18},"llm":{"key":"02f487d0-004a-488c-b0e8-716165011454","name":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite","model":"google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"12b689fd-8b31-426a-8e0c-6fb531f01687","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":42,"LLM_1":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Are cats and dogs different species?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes, cats and dogs are definitely different species. In fact, they belong to entirely different taxonomic families.\n\nHere is the scientific breakdown of why they are different:\n\n*   **Domestic Cat:** Belongs to the family **Felidae** and the species *Felis catus*.\n*   **Domestic Dog:** Belongs to the family **Canidae** and the species *Canis lupus familiaris*.\n\nWhile they both belong to the same biological **order** (**Carnivora**), suggesting they share a common ancestor deep in their evolutionary history, their lineages diverged approximately 40 to 50 million years ago. Because they are different species within different families, they cannot interbreed to produce offspring.","reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a1+ih2dd/5xoqT99LPjpDs6JGCL8KVz3MdjwqQZamVxDO9ntRF1R7b7Va0Sk8O8uAGH1A4tCsHakHvCh09KJ3pbgxh9t6LzJQLxde7atG50=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}}],"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a19tiAt/MsMJ6nDhDWwvuHfxXyeIpUyPQeksYTHPfPtnIrvgj22BIaql/NLRUHHpIVNU2tLmmm0yg0QywM7EdwdlNiiKCuESHLSt8Jxk3S8=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},{"text":97,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":29},"llm":{"key":"02f487d0-004a-488c-b0e8-716165011454","name":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite","model":"google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"004fee61-1255-4404-8ada-b4fc26e8ec40","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":42,"LLM_1":"Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Who invented the lightbulb?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The invention of the lightbulb is often attributed to **Thomas Edison**, but the reality is that the lightbulb was the result of a long process involving many different inventors over several decades.\n\nHere is a breakdown of the history:\n\n*   **Early Pioneers (Before Edison):** As early as 1802, Humphry Davy invented the first electric light (the arc lamp). Throughout the 1800s, many inventors—such as Warren de la Rue, Joseph Swan, and James Bowman Lindsay—created various forms of electric lights. However, these were generally impractical, short-lived, or too expensive for home use.\n*   **Joseph Swan:** Perhaps the most important predecessor to Edison was the British physicist Joseph Swan. By 1878, Swan had developed a working lightbulb using a carbonized paper filament. He received a British patent for it in 1880, shortly before Edison received his.\n*   **Thomas Edison:** Edison's major contribution, beginning in 1879, was not just the bulb itself, but the **entire electrical system** required to make it practical. He identified a carbonized bamboo filament that could burn for over 1,200 hours, and he developed the vacuum pumps, generators, and wiring grids necessary to bring electricity into homes and businesses. \n\n**The Conclusion:**\nWhile Thomas Edison is credited with the \"invention\" of the commercially viable, long-lasting incandescent lightbulb, it is more accurate to say that he **perfected** it. Because of their competing patents, Edison and Swan eventually joined forces to form the company \"Ediswan,\" which manufactured the bulbs in Britain.","reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a1/QBDunney1QOo/szBDChDlLArbXf+YQVlhsFml53EvoeArWI7sFcma547BttBB+JMRicPb55o19zIBvjyaMGEj08u/fA8NU8XI2z59lYA=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}}],"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"AY89a1/4qQWF9olyGP7MseoR5O24Nmhs3YvTXEJxImh8PHy9Totz7gV7cMhjN9rUyw/NM+mm+yWxNro6CkfOGeJ7i4LIWg92L2ULTqg5QV18B6c=","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},{"text":121,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":18},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"be2fc961-ed8b-4f51-9b63-a1c40c59420b","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Are cats and dogs different species?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes, cats and dogs are different species. They belong to different biological genera and families: cats are *Felis catus* (family Felidae), while dogs are *Canis lupus familiaris* (family Canidae). They cannot interbreed to produce offspring, which is one of the key definitions of separate species."}]},{"text":139,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":5},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"8bf5a753-9c17-4e36-94fc-83fe46303272","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"What is the capital of France?"},{"role":"assistant","content":" The capital of France is Paris."}]},{"text":144,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":29},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"8d46919b-e122-4864-968d-14a787d7f4ec","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Who invented the lightbulb?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The invention of the lightbulb is most famously credited to **Thomas Edison**, who developed a practical and commercially viable incandescent lightbulb in 1879. However, he didn't invent it from scratch—he improved on earlier designs.\n\nKey contributors before Edison include:\n- **Humphry Davy** (1802): Demonstrated the principle of electric light with a carbon arc lamp.\n- **Warren de la Rue** (1840): Built an early incandescent lamp using a platinum filament (too expensive for practical use).\n- **Joseph Swan** (1878): Patented a working incandescent lamp in the UK using a carbon filament. Swan and Edison later merged their companies.\n\nSo, while Edison is often credited due to his patented design, better filament materials, and the development of a full electrical system to make the bulb practical for homes, the reality is a collaborative evolution."}]},{"text":146,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":2},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"93e3c88f-48a7-4257-aaf4-3c7e0db4e56c","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"What is 2+2?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"2+2 equals 4."}]},{"text":147,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":15},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"f4c94d92-1a7e-4d4b-bee2-ba5a1136010f","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Is the Legend of Zelda a video game series?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes, **The Legend of Zelda** is a highly influential and critically acclaimed video game series created by Nintendo. It debuted in 1986 with the original game for the Nintendo Entertainment System (NES). The series primarily follows the adventures of Link, a courageous hero, as he battles the evil Ganon and rescues Princess Zelda in the fantasy land of Hyrule. Known for its action-adventure gameplay, puzzle-solving, exploration, and iconic music, the series has produced numerous celebrated titles across multiple Nintendo consoles."}]},{"text":149,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":8},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"8609471f-eb7c-4ef9-9893-0c8f439f648e","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"What year was the U.S. Declaration of Independence adopted?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The U.S. Declaration of Independence was adopted on July 4, 1776."}]},{"text":155,"prompt":39,"fill_history":{"complaint":39,"question":26},"llm":{"key":"2cbcc4e4-fa35-413e-83a0-165794039102","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":85.71428571428571,"error":0}},"uid":"1e5d00b2-aec3-42e8-95fa-810e96412e19","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":122,"LLM_1":"DeepSeek V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Where was the computer first invented?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The concept of the computer evolved over time, and the first mechanical computer is often credited to **Charles Babbage**, an English mathematician, who designed the **Difference Engine** in the 1820s and later the more general **Analytical Engine** in the 1830s. These were created in **England**.\n\nHowever, the first **electronic general-purpose computer**, known as the **ENIAC** (Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer), was developed in the **United States** at the University of Pennsylvania, completing in 1945. So, depending on your definition, the answer could be **England** (for mechanical computers) or the **United States** (for modern electronic computers)."}]},{"text":83,"prompt":48,"fill_history":{"complaint":48,"question":2},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"41893f1a-cb5d-4753-9d6e-3a9f6fcac7af","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":67,"LLM_1":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"What is 2+2?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"2 + 2 = 4"}]},{"text":85,"prompt":48,"fill_history":{"complaint":48,"question":5},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openroute