"The U.S. Declaration of Independence was adopted on July 4, 1776."}]},{"text":109,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":2},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"955c35a7-ec0a-4260-952a-c5a4c7c9e8aa","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":67,"LLM_1":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"What is 2+2?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"2 + 2 = 4"}]},{"text":119,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":26},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"58bc41e5-dcc9-48d9-9527-849442a43e03","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":67,"LLM_1":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Where was the computer first invented?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"# The Computer's Origins\n\nThere's no single location where computers were \"invented,\" as the development was gradual and international:\n\n## Key Early Locations:\n\n- **England**: Charles Babbage designed the **Analytical Engine** (1830s-40s) in London, considered a precursor to modern computers.\n\n- **Germany**: Konrad Zuse built the **Z1** (1938) in Berlin, often credited as the first programmable digital computer.\n\n- **United States**: \n  - The **ENIAC** (1945) was built at the University of Pennsylvania\n  - Alan Turing worked on computer theory in Britain but influenced development worldwide\n\n- **Britain**: Early stored-program computers like the **Manchester Mark 1** (1948) were developed.\n\n## Bottom Line:\n\nIf you're asking about **programmable digital computers**, credit is typically shared between **Germany** (Zuse's Z1) and the **United States** (ENIAC), with important theoretical work done in **Britain**. The invention was more of a collective, international achievement than a single discovery in one place."}]},{"text":129,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":15},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"82506fe3-8008-4ec3-9d3c-903b93045b47","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":67,"LLM_1":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Is the Legend of Zelda a video game series?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes, the Legend of Zelda is a video game series. It's one of Nintendo's most iconic and beloved franchises, featuring action-adventure games that began with the original \"The Legend of Zelda\" released in 1986 for the Nintendo Entertainment System (NES). The series has since expanded to numerous games across various Nintendo platforms, with popular titles including \"Ocarina of Time,\" \"Breath of the Wild,\" and \"Tears of the Kingdom.\""}]},{"text":131,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":18},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"4c4be656-fd16-4b49-845e-cbbc1f6593e4","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":67,"LLM_1":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Are cats and dogs different species?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes, cats and dogs are different species. They belong to different genera within the family Carnivora:\n\n- **Cats** (genus *Felis* for domestic cats, though there are other cat genera) are felids\n- **Dogs** (genus *Canis* for domestic dogs) are canids\n\nThey cannot interbreed to produce fertile offspring, which is one of the key biological definitions of being separate species. While they're both carnivorous mammals and share a common ancestor from millions of years ago, they've evolved distinct characteristics, behaviors, and biology over time."}]},{"text":137,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":29},"llm":{"key":"709bcbeb-dc76-426c-bbce-9e2551720716","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"1671ab27-6f5e-44de-be23-a2e1de90cf1e","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":67,"LLM_1":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Who invented the lightbulb?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Thomas Edison is most famously credited with inventing the practical lightbulb in 1879. He developed a long-lasting incandescent bulb with a carbonized cotton filament that could burn for many hours.\n\nHowever, it's worth noting that the invention was built on work by earlier inventors. Joseph Swan in Britain and Humphry Davy had also experimented with electric light in the 1800s. Edison's key achievement was creating a reliable, commercially viable bulb that could be mass-produced and used in homes and businesses."}]},{"text":82,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":2},"llm":{"key":"10341d13-09b9-4354-993b-fcb8940245e1","name":"GPT-5.4 Mini","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.4-mini","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"GPT-5.4 Mini","model":"openai/gpt-5.4-mini","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"d544010c-a8f8-4195-a1d2-fd45ad6803dd","metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":46,"LLM_1":"GPT-5.4 Mini"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"What is 2+2?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"2 + 2 = 4."}]},{"text":100,"prompt":58,"fill_history":{"complaint":58,"question":5},"llm":{"key":"10341d13-09b9-4354-993b-fcb8940245e1","name":"GPT-5.4 Mini","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.4-mini","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortnam