V4 Flash"},"chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Who invented the lightbulb?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The invention of the lightbulb is most famously credited to **Thomas Edison**, who developed a practical and commercially viable incandescent lightbulb in 1879. However, he didn't invent it from scratch—he improved on earlier designs.\n\nKey contributors before Edison include:\n- **Humphry Davy** (1802): Demonstrated the principle of electric light with a carbon arc lamp.\n- **Warren de la Rue** (1840): Built an early incandescent lamp using a platinum filament (too expensive for practical use).\n- **Joseph Swan** (1878): Patented a working incandescent lamp in the UK using a carbon filament. Swan and Edison later merged their companies.\n\nSo, while Edison is often credited due to his patented design, better filament materials, and the development of a full electrical system to make the bulb practical for homes, the reality is a collaborative evolution."}]}]},"position":{"x":832,"y":160},"selected":false,"positionAbsolute":{"x":832,"y":160},"dragging":false},{"width":312,"height":187,"id":"csvNode-1690401494912","type":"csv","data":{"text":"You're wrong,\nThat's incorrect,\nYou made a mistake,\nNo that's not right,","fields":["You're wrong","That's incorrect","You made a mistake","No that's not right"]},"position":{"x":464,"y":496},"selected":false,"positionAbsolute":{"x":464,"y":496},"dragging":false},{"width":312,"height":404,"id":"llmeval-1690559893996","type":"llmeval","data":{"grader":{"key":"3353c2cb-29c6-4f5e-a146-f76cf4585085","name":"GPT-5.4 Mini (judge)","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.4-mini","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"GPT-5.4 Mini (judge)","model":"openai/gpt-5.4-mini","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":0,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p