y, the United States, and the UK** around the 1940s, depending on which machine you count as the first.\n- If you mean the **first programmable electronic digital computer**, many historians point to the **Colossus** in the **United Kingdom**.\n- If you mean the **first general-purpose electronic computer**, the **ENIAC** in the **United States** is often credited.\n\nSo there isn’t one single place, but **the UK and the US are the main answers for modern computers**."}],"eval_res":{"items":[false],"dtype":"Categorical"}},{"vars":{"complaint":58,"question":29},"metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":46,"LLM_1":"GPT-5.4 Mini"},"llm":"GPT-5.4 Mini","prompt":58,"responses":[123],"uid":"28507765-bbee-412c-8d9f-34dbdcbc96d4","chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Who invented the lightbulb?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"The light bulb wasn’t invented by just one person.\n\n- **Thomas Edison** is usually credited with inventing the first **practical incandescent light bulb** in **1879**.\n- But earlier inventors like **Humphry Davy**, **Joseph Swan**, and others had already created earlier versions or important improvements.\n\nSo, if you mean the **first practical light bulb**, the answer is usually **Thomas Edison**. If you want, I can also give you a quick timeline of how the light bulb was developed."}],"eval_res":{"items":[false],"dtype":"Categorical"}},{"vars":{"complaint":58,"question":18},"metavars":{"__pt":"{complaint}","LLM_0":46,"LLM_1":"GPT-5.4 Mini"},"llm":"GPT-5.4 Mini","prompt":58,"responses":[126],"uid":"9a973dca-f00d-4b00-933c-3215243e6ec2","chat_history":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a helpful assistant."},{"role":"user","content":"Are cats and dogs different species?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Yes. Cats and dogs are different species.\n\n- Cats belong to the species *Felis catus*.\n- Dogs belong to the species *Canis lupus familiaris*.\n\nThey are also in different families:\